{
  "content": "<h1><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"InventoryUnitCosts\">Inventory Unit Costs</span></h1><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Date InventoryItem InventoryItems InventoryUnitCost InventoryUnitCosts Item On To ToDate UnitCost\">The <strong>Inventory Unit Costs</strong> screen enables you to manage unit costs for your inventory items at specific dates.</p><div class=\"flex pointer-events-none space-x-6 rtl:space-x-reverse items-center\"><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 inline-block ltr:pr-8 rtl:pl-8\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-200 ltr:pl-8 rtl:pr-8\"><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div><div class=\"border-y ltr:border-l rtl:border-r border-neutral-300 bg-white p-4 flex gap-2 items-center\"><i class=\"fas fa-cog text-neutral-400\"></i><span class=\"font-semibold text-sm text-[#428bca]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"Settings\">Settings</span></span></div><div class=\"border-x border-neutral-300 bg-neutral-100 h-2\"></div></div></div><span class=\"rtl:hidden\"><i class=\"fas fa-circle-chevron-right text-lg text-neutral-300\"></i></span><span class=\"ltr:hidden\"><i class=\"fas fa-circle-chevron-left text-lg text-neutral-300\"></i></span><div class=\"border rounded inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"basis-72 flex items-center gap-2 p-4\"><i class=\"text-xl text-neutral-400 fas fa-fw fa-scanner-keyboard\"></i><span class=\"text-sm text-[#428bca]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"InventoryUnitCosts\">Inventory Unit Costs</span></span></div></div></div><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action Find From FromDate InventoryItem Is Item Off On ProductionOrder To ToDate Transaction UnitCost\">When you sell, write off, or use an inventory item in a production order, Manager will find the unit cost from this screen to match with your inventory transaction.</p><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Manual\">Manual Entry</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Create InventoryUnitCost NewInventoryUnitCost On To ToDate UnitCost\">To create a new inventory unit cost, click the <strong>New Inventory Unit Cost</strong> button.</p><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"mt-4 ms-4 pe-8 items-center bg-neutral-100 p-4 border-neutral-200 border-s border-t rounded-ss-lg flex gap-4 shadow-[inset_0px_1px_0px_#fff]\"><span class=\"text-base font-bold text-neutral-300 [text-shadow:_1px_1px_0px_#fff]\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"InventoryUnitCosts\">Inventory Unit Costs</span></span><span class=\"text-neutral-300 hover:text-neutral-400\"><i class=\"fas fa-square-question\" style=\"font-size: 16px\"></i></span><span class=\"bg-white text-neutral-700 border border-neutral-300 font-semibold rounded-md py-2 px-4 text-sm\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"NewInventoryUnitCost\">New Inventory Unit Cost</span></span></div></div><h2 translate=\"true\" keywords=\"To ToDate\">Automated Cost Management</h2><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"InventoryCostCorrection InventoryUnitCost InventoryUnitCosts Is Manual On To ToDate UnitCost\">However, instead of creating inventory unit costs manually, use the <strong>Inventory Cost Correction</strong> screen to automate this task.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"Action And Calculation CostOfSales Create Date Delete InventoryCostCorrection InventoryUnitCost InventoryUnitCosts On Rate Sales To ToDate Transaction Transactions UnitCost Update\">The <strong>Inventory Cost Correction</strong> screen analyzes all your transactions and suggests which inventory unit costs should be created, updated, or deleted so that your <em>cost of sales</em> calculations are accurate.</p><p translate=\"true\" keywords=\"InventoryCostCorrection On To ToDate\">To access the <strong>Inventory Cost Correction</strong> screen, click the <strong>Inventory Cost Correction</strong> button in the bottom-right corner.</p><div class=\"border rounded p-0.5 pb-4 inline-block pointer-events-none\"><div class=\"bg-neutral-100 p-3 border-b\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-4\"><span class=\"border text-xs rounded py-1 px-2 bg-white border-neutral-300 text-neutral-400\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"InventoryCostCorrection\">Inventory Cost Correction</span></span></div></div></div><p><span translate=\"true\" keywords=\"On\">For more information, see:</span> <a href=\"/guides/inventory-cost-correction\"><span translate=\"true\" keyword=\"InventoryCostCorrection\">Inventory Cost Correction</span></a></p>",
  "key": "inventory-unit-costs"
}
